# Copy to .env at the repo root (gitignored). Used by scripts/smoke.ts (`cd scripts; npm run smoke`).
# Project Settings → API in the Supabase dashboard. The service role key bypasses RLS: it never
# goes into the app, a build, or CI logs. Point this at a dedicated smoke/staging project: the
# smoke test leaves a settled group behind (docs/DEPLOY.md, "Smoke test").
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=YOUR-SERVICE-ROLE-KEY

# The app reads its own app/.env (EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY); see app/.env.example.

# Strava (Edge Function strava-sync; docs/DEPLOY.md "Strava"). These are FUNCTION secrets, set with
# `supabase secrets set NAME=value`, never EXPO_PUBLIC_ and never in the app. Listed here only so
# the names live in one place; scripts/smoke.ts does not read them.
# STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=            # strava.com/settings/api → Client ID
# STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET=        # strava.com/settings/api → Client Secret
# STRAVA_VERIFY_TOKEN=         # random string; Strava echoes it on the webhook handshake
# STRAVA_STATE_SECRET=         # random 32+ bytes; signs the OAuth state
# APP_SCHEME=finalcall         # optional
# WEB_ORIGIN=https://ishaanmakam.github.io   # optional; comma-separated origins allowed as web redirects
# STRAVA_FUNCTION_URL=         # optional; public URL of the function when SUPABASE_URL is not it (local serve)
